is are Trump's lawyers going to use the same&nbsp;
stupid arguments that they're making on TV&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.580 --> 00:00:26.400
when it comes to courts of law? Because if they&nbsp;
do, it's going to be very embarrassing for them.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:32.100
I'm going to give you one such example. Here&nbsp;
is Trump attorney Christina Bobb, who was on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.100 --> 00:00:41.040
Newsmax two days ago, I believe it was. And she&nbsp;
started making the case that the raid was illegal&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:41.580 --> 00:00:47.580
and that it's unconstitutional and that&nbsp;
privileged documents were taken. It's a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:47.580 --> 00:00:53.640
very dumb argument. Is she willing to make it&nbsp;
in court or do they only make these arguments&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.640 --> 00:00:57.600
for the court of public opinion on TV?
Speaker 4: Oh no, that anything about this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.600 --> 00:01:03.480
raid was legal. But they did take attorney client&nbsp;
documents. We know that because in the warrant,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:03.480 --> 00:01:07.320
in the receipt of property that they gave us,&nbsp;
they actually gave us two separate receipts&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:07.320 --> 00:01:10.620
of property. One of them is a shorter list.&nbsp;
I think it only has about five or six items&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.620 --> 00:01:14.760
on it. And then you've got the other one that&nbsp;
has the, I don't know, 20 or so items on it.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:14.760 --> 00:01:20.100
And the shorter list, which doesn't explain that&nbsp;
it's privileged information, they just happened&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.100 --> 00:01:24.420
to tell me that when they gave me the receipt,&nbsp;
they said, this is privileged information that,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:24.420 --> 00:01:28.380
you know, we're handling it differently. You&nbsp;
know, we'll work out with the lawyers how to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:28.380 --> 00:01:33.180
handle it. But of course, you know, they write out&nbsp;
classified information on the one list. And then&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.180 --> 00:01:38.460
when they take something that is questionable&nbsp;
and the public won't like, they leave that off&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:38.460 --> 00:01:42.960
of the list and just tell me. So I think it's&nbsp;
a lot of gamesmanship. I think what they did&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.960 --> 00:01:47.509
is wrong. It's illegal, it's unconstitutional.&nbsp;
And I think they have a lot of explaining to do.&nbsp;

